# Task 2 – Data Representation

## 1. Vehicle

| Attribute | Data Type |
|---|---|
| registrationNo | String |
| vehicleType | String |
| ownerType | String |

## 2. ParkingSlot

| Attribute | Data Type |
|---|---|
| floorNo | int |
| slotNo | int |
| slotType | String |
| isAvailable | boolean |

## 3. ParkingTicket

| Attribute | Data Type |
|---|---|
| ticketId | String |
| vehicleNo | String |
| floorNo | int |
| slotNo | int |
| entryTime | String |
| exitTime | String |
| fee | double |

## 4. ParkingFacility

| Attribute | Data Type |
|---|---|
| numberOfFloors | int |
| slotsPerFloor | int[] |
## 5. Representation Choice

- `String` is used for vehicle registration numbers and ticket IDs.
- `int` is used for floor and slot numbers.
- `boolean` is used to represent whether a parking slot is available.
- `double` is used for parking fee because the fee may contain decimal values.
- `int[]` is used to store the number of slots available on each floor.
